      "dom_id": "question-115488",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Consider the table below. Which of the following is a true statement about the relationship between $x$ and $y?$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $0.5$ | $20$ |\n| $2$ | $5$ |\n| $4$ | $2.5$ |",
      "worked_solution": "If $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ then we must have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{k}{x}.\n$$\n\nfor some constant $k.$ Note that we can rewrite the above equation as follows.\n\n$$\nx\\cdot y=k\n$$\n\nSo, we will compute $x\\cdot y=k$ for each row in the table. If we get the same value of $k$ for each row, then we can conclude that $y$ is inversely proportional to $x.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $x\\cdot y=k$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0.5$ | $20$ | $0.5\\cdot 20=10$ |\n| $2$ | $5$ | $2\\cdot 5=10$ |\n| $4$ | $2.5$ | $4\\cdot 2.5=10$ |\n\nThe results are all the same: in each row, we have $k=10.$ Therefore, $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ and the constant of variation is $k=10.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
